{"session_id":"b49f5c4e-6bf8-4b8d-8ef9-1f7f8fafc561","transcript_path":"/Users/scolladon/.claude/projects/-Users-scolladon-workspace-perso-craft-bash32-heredoc-commit-idiom/b49f5c4e-6bf8-4b8d-8ef9-1f7f8fafc561.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/scolladon/workspace/perso/craft-bash32-heredoc-commit-idiom","scratchpad_dir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-scolladon-workspace-perso-craft/b49f5c4e-6bf8-4b8d-8ef9-1f7f8fafc561/scratchpad","prompt_id":"0548b6c4-2694-4257-ae74-735511365224","permission_mode":"auto","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PermissionRequest","tool_name":"AskUserQuestion","tool_input":{"questions":[{"question":"DC-1 — Under macOS /bin/bash 3.2, `git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF' … EOF)\"` breaks: an odd ' \" ` or ( gives a syntax error, and a ) silently ends the message early. Craft never teaches this idiom; the harness defaults (Claude Code, copilot) do. How should craft respond?","header":"Commit form","options":[{"label":"Teach in core (Recommended)","description":"Add one line to contracts/core.md, which every phase spawn gets in both agent and inline mode: commit with git commit -m \"<msg>\" (one double-quoted -m per paragraph), or -F <file> when the message holds \" $ ` \\ !. Never use the heredoc idiom. Also add a CORE_MARKERS pin and the docs. Costs about 240 bytes per spawn."},{"label":"Document only","description":"Only copilot README and gate.md gain the workaround. No contract change; roles keep the harness default, which fails or writes a wrong message on bash 3.2."},{"label":"Teach in bundles","description":"Put the same line in the producer/construction/refinement/harness-exec/delivery bundles. Review spawns skip it, but the rule is repeated 5 times, and the decisions phase, which commits ADRs and has no bundle, never gets it."}],"multiSelect":false},{"question":"DC-2 — SECURITY: copilot's plain-command gate accepts the idiom and treats its body as data. I reproduced the following myself: `git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'⏎x)\"; git branch -D victim; echo \"⏎EOF⏎)\"` is ALLOWED by copilotGuard, and /bin/bash 3.2 then deleted branch `victim` in a throwaway repo. Plain `git branch -D victim` is DENIED. zsh keeps the branch. Not run live through copilot. What should the gate do?","header":"Copilot gate","options":[{"label":"Deny the idiom (Recommended)","description":"Delete the idiom special case in git-plain-command-gate.js. The idiom then falls under the existing deny for `$` inside double quotes. Fails closed, removes code, and costs one re-issue in the taught form. Needs a refining ADR on ADR-595."},{"label":"Keep, list as residual","description":"Keep accepting the idiom and document the bash-3.2 early-close smuggle as an accepted residual. Smallest change; the bypass stays open."},{"label":"Allow safe bodies only","description":"Accept the idiom only when the body has no ' \" ` ( ). This needs a character set pinned against bash 3.2's scanner, any gap fails open, and it denies most real bodies anyway."}],"multiSelect":false}]}}
